   ],
   "customData": {
    "author": "agent",
    "kind": "entity",
    "role": "node",
    "tooltip": "**'scored at' is mine, and it is a direct consequence of the partial-rerun finding.**\n\nA single-pipeline rerun re-scores one pass and leaves the other three alone, so a run's Signals can come from two different moments. In the model as drawn, that situation was *unrepresentable* — which is a decent explanation of how it went unnoticed for so long.\n\nWith a scoring time on the Signal, mixed provenance becomes something the system can state instead of something it merely does."
   },
   "fillStyle": "solid",
